 okay . and when was your last pap smear ?\n[patient] uh , about six months ago . it came back normal , though .\n[doctor] okay . good , okay . well , let\'s see ... let\'s take a look at you , and then , we\'ll get some samples for std testing . okay ?\n[patient] all right .\n[doctor] you\'ll hear me talk through your exam , so that i can get it all documented . uh- ?\n[doctor] use my general physical exam template . pelvic exam demonstrates no external lesions . normal labia majora and labia minora . normal physiological discharge , with normal color and smell .\n[doctor] ms. ross , i\'m going to touch you , now . you\'ll feel my fingers , and the speculum in your vagina . you\'ll feel some pressure , now .\n[doctor] cervix is normal . vaginal wall is normal . no cervical motion tenderness and no adnexal tenderness or masses noted . swabs were done for std testing .\n[doctor] okay , ms. ross . everything looks good from a visual standpoint . i\'m going to send off std testing for , uh , gonorrhea , chlamydia , trichomoniasis , and i\'ll have you give some blood for syphilis , hiv and hepatitis c. some of these tests will take longer than others . we will call you , if we see anything , but if you have n\'t heard anything , you can call us in three days for results .\n[patient] okay . sounds good . thank you , so much .\n[doctor] of course , my pleasure . and , if everything is normal , i\'ll see you again , at your next annual checkup .\n[doctor] assessment : is screen for std .\n[doctor] plan : discussed with patient , and please add that she is high risk due to an abnormal pap smear in the past , and the recent discovery of her sexual partner having multiple partners , for some period of time .\n[doctor] end of recording .\n#############################\n\n\n###Response A:\n{{ CHIEF COMPLAINT\n\nFull spectrum std testing.\n\nHISTORY OF PRESENT ILLNESS\n\nGrace Ross is a 25-year-old female who presents today for full spectrum std testing. The patient states that she is experiencing symptoms of discomfort, a change in discharge, and odor in her vaginal region. She reports that the right side of her vagina is starting to become painful. The patient denies fevers or chills. She reports that she recently learned her partner has been in sexual encounters with other people and she wants to be evaluated for all stds.\n\nMEDICAL HISTORY\n\nThe patient reports she recently had an irregular pap smear at age 20. She has not had one since. She last had a pap smear 6 months ago, which was normal.\n\nSOCIAL HISTORY\n\nThe patient reports she has been dating for 3 years. She recently learned that her partner has been having multiple sexual partners over the past 3 months.\n\nPHYSICAL EXAM\n\nPelvic exam demonstrates no external lesions. Normal labia majora and labia minora. Normal physiological discharge with normal color and smell. Cervix is normal. Vaginal wall is normal. No cervical motion tenderness and no adnexal tenderness or masses noted. Swabs were done for std testing.\n\nASSESSMENT\n\n• Screening for std.\n\nPLAN\n\nI have had a lengthy discussion with the patient today. I have advised that we will call her if we see anything, but if she has not heard from us, she can call in 3 days for results. If everything is normal, I will see her again at her next annual check-up.\n\nINSTRUCTIONS\n\nWe will call her if we see anything. If she has not heard from us, she can call in 3 days for results. She will see me again at her next annual check-up.\n\nCLINICAL NOTES\n\nThe patient was very cooperative and in agreement with the plan. }}<|eot_id|>\n\n###Response B:\n{{ CHIEF COMPLAINT\n\nFull spectrum std testing.\n\nHISTORY OF PRESENT ILLNESS\n\nMs. Ross is a 24-year-old female who presents today for full spectrum std testing. She states she has been experiencing symptoms of discomfort, a change in discharge, and odor in her vaginal region. She notes that the right side of her vagina is starting to become painful. She denies any fevers or 