tion and adduction to 90 degrees. Pain with supination and pronation of the right arm.\n\nRESULTS\n\nX-ray of the right shoulder was obtained today and revealed an acute AC joint fracture.\n\nASSESSMENT AND PLAN\n\nMatthew Thompson is a 67-year-old male who presents to the clinic today for the evaluation of right shoulder pain. After reviewing the patient\'s examination and radiographic findings, I have diagnosed him with an acute AC joint fracture.\n\nThe patient will be placed in a sling for comfort. I will prescribe Meloxicam 15 mg once a day. We will order a CT scan of the right shoulder for further evaluation. We will refer the patient to physical therapy to strengthen his shoulder in hopes of avoiding surgery in the future.\n\nPatient Agreements: The patient understands and agrees with the recommended medical treatment plan.\n\nINSTRUCTIONS\n\nThe patient will follow up with me in 1 week for re-evaluation. }}<|eot_id|>\n\n###Response B:\n{{ CHIEF COMPLAINT\n\nRight shoulder pain.\n\nHISTORY OF PRESENT ILLNESS\n\nMatthew Johnson is a 67-year-old male who presents to the clinic today for an evaluation of right shoulder pain. The onset of the pain occurred 4 days ago when he was playing tackle football. The patient states he was tackled and landed on his right shoulder. He states he was able to get back into the game but the pain has been bothering him since then. The patient denies any numbness or tingling in his fingers and denies any problems with the strength of his arm. He is right handed and states he is able to grab a cup of coffee. He reports that he is right handed and denies any problems with lifting his shoulder to his ear. The patient states he has been taking Tylenol, but it has not provided relief from his pain. The patient states his neck has been okay and he denies any other joint problems. He states he has had an appendectomy for appendicitis 3 to 4 years ago. The patient is currently playing flag football.\n\nREVIEW OF SYSTEMS\n\nConstitutional: